{
  "manufacturer": "Intesis (HMS Networks)",
  "manufacturer_slug": "intesis",
  "model": "IN485MIT001A000 Mitsubishi Electric Ecodan air-to-water to Modbus RTU / BACnet MS/TP gateway",
  "model_slug": "in485mit001a000",
  "short_model": "IN485MIT001A000",
  "aliases": [
    "IN485MIT001A000",
    "Ecodan Modbus",
    "Mitsubishi Ecodan Modbus RTU",
    "Intesis Ecodan",
    "HMS Ecodan gateway"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Heat pump gateway (VRF / split AC gateway)",
  "applies_to": "Intesis (HMS Networks) IN485MIT001A000 gateway on the CN105 socket of Mitsubishi Electric Ecodan air-to-water heat pumps, set to Modbus RTU, per user manual version 1.0.3 (2025-12-02).",
  "summary": "This Intesis gateway plugs into the CN105 connector of a Mitsubishi Electric Ecodan air-to-water heat pump and makes it a Modbus RTU server (or a BACnet MS/TP device, chosen by DIP switch). All points are single 16-bit holding registers: system on/off, heat/cool mode, Zone 1 and Zone 2 setpoints and control type, DHW setpoint, eco and boost, water temperatures, compressor and pump status, run hours, flow and energy counters, plus error codes.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 2400,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The manual gives each register a 'Modbus address (base 0)' and a 'PLC address (base 1)' column. This map uses the base-0 value as the wire address, so On/off is address 130 (PLC 131)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "IN485MIT001A000 User Manual - Mitsubishi Electric Ecodan Air-to-Water Units to BACnet MS/TP and Modbus RTU",
    "doc_number": "User Manual Version 1.0.3",
    "revision_date": "2025-12-02",
    "url": "https://www.hms-networks.com/docs/default-source/products/intesis/manuals-and-guides---manuals/user-manual-in485mit001a000.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 7-8 (DIP switches), pp. 10-11 (wiring), p. 26 (functions, physical layer), pp. 27-36 (register tables), p. 37 (virtual temperature), p. 40 (error codes)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Temperatures follow DIP switch SW2: position 7 OFF = whole degrees (x1, factory default), ON = tenths (x10, 19.2 = 192); position 8 OFF = °C (default), ON = °F. Units and scale here are for the defaults; use scale 0.1 if you set x10.",
    "Every register starts at 0x8000 (-32768) until the gateway has read the unit; the manual writes this value as negative, so temperatures are typed signed 16-bit.",
    "An invalid write resets a temperature register to 0x8000; other registers keep their old value.",
    "Zone 2 custom, unit and applied limit registers (241-252) mirror Zone 1's (161-172) and are left out to keep the map short; so are the Zone 1 unit limits (165-168), DHW applied limits (281-282) and the gateway-only registers not needed for control.",
    "Error code (108) is the code shown on Mitsubishi centralised controllers and sub code (109) the Ecodan screen code, both as hex digits in a 16-bit value (e.g. 0x0601 reads 1537 in decimal); the conversion table is in section 10 of the manual."
  ],
